title: keybindings-variables panel
tags: Panel [[Panel types]] [[Customising the GUI]] Keybindings
kind: reference
summary: Every variable of keybindings.toml, filtered by key or name: its value, edited in place, the keys it stands for, and how many lines use it.

Open it with `panel:open here keybindings-variables` (<<key "panel:open here keybindings-variables" "t k v">>).
It lists every variable of the file, in its order: its name, its value — a field —, the
keys it stands for, and how many lines use it, directly or through another variable
([[Keybinding variables]]).

The filter above the list narrows it as it is typed: first the variables whose keys
start with the text — `shift+m`, however the chord is written —, then those
whose name holds it. <<key "keybindings-variables:focus filter" "p e">> gives it the focus;
opening the panel does not.

What a new value would do is said as it is typed — how many keys change, or why it is
refused: a key bound twice, or a key alone hiding a sequence that nothing hid before.
''Enter'' writes it, in its line of the file; ''Escape'' gives the old value back.

The list is read again when the panel is shown, at `view:refresh`, and when the
[[keybindings panel]] of the workspace changes a line; a value written here makes that
panel read its lines again in turn.
